  "notes": "Aladin Lite v3 sky atlas. UI chrome is deliberately utilitarian: light grey #ececec boxes with 2px dark #212121 borders, 3px radii, 30px square icon buttons (eye/gear/trash/download), monospace everywhere; the active tool has a green #008000 border. Search box shows current RA/Dec in magenta #ff54ff. Overlay rows carry a small coloured legend glyph matching each catalogue's marker colour/shape (SIMBAD red circles, OriB YSO green diamonds, Gaia orange squares, notes yellow dots, footprint colours). Survey layers stack with blend/opacity/delete controls; PanSTARRS layer is hidden (crossed eye). Live check: clicking a note marker opens a pinned popover card ('sigma Ori cluster' note with close ×) and a SIMBAD results table docks at the bottom-left — not visible in the capture. Projection 'SIN' and FoV readout '3.600° × 2.250°'."
